### =========================================================================
### 🎓 LOGGING — Pino + request ID
### 📅 Day 42 · Phase 9 (Pangunahing hardening)
### =========================================================================
### Bawat request ay may sariling ID (X-Request-Id sa sagot) at isang linya ng
### log kapag tapos na: { requestId, clientIp, req, res.statusCode, responseTime }.
###
### 👀 Buksan ang terminal ng `npm run dev` habang nagse-send — doon lumalabas ang logs
###    (may kulay sa dev: pino-pretty · JSON sa production: `docker compose logs backend`).
###
### 🔐 HINDI kailanman lalabas sa log: password, cookie (JWT), Authorization, Set-Cookie.
###
### Code: backend/src/lib/logger.ts · backend/src/middleware/requestLogger.ts
### Test: lib/logger.test.ts · middleware/requestLogger.test.ts · routes/requestId.test.ts
### Diagram: docs/diagrams/01-request-lifecycle.md
### =========================================================================

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Kahit anong request. Ang inaasahan:
###    Header: X-Request-Id: <uuid>   (hal. 6e4305bb-7628-4b02-9a91-7432652b2c0b)
###    401 kung hindi pa naka-login (200 pagkatapos ng #2)
###    Terminal: WARN request completed · requestId: <PAREHONG uuid> · statusCode: 401
###
### 🔍 Kopyahin ang X-Request-Id → hanapin sa terminal (Ctrl+F) → ang eksaktong log ng request na ito
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/me

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Mag-login (ang account mula sa 05-login.http — i-register muna roon kung wala pa). Ang inaasahan:
###    200 · sa terminal: POST /api/auth/login · statusCode: 200
###    🔐 WALA ang password sa log, at WALA ang token (sinubukan: 0 match, Day 42)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "login-demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Maling password. Ang inaasahan:
###    401 · sa terminal: WARN (dilaw) — 4xx = mali ang client · 5xx = ERROR (pula) = sira ang server
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "login-demo@example.com",
  "password": "mali-ito"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Pekeng X-Request-Id mula sa client. Ang inaasahan:
###    Ang X-Request-Id sa sagot ay BAGONG uuid — HINDI "ako-ang-magpapasya"
###    🔐 Kapareho ng aral sa CF-Connecting-IP: huwag pagkatiwalaan ang header na kayang pekein
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/me
X-Request-Id: ako-ang-magpapasya

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Health check. Ang inaasahan:
###    200 · pero WALANG log sa terminal — tinatawag ito ng Docker HEALTHCHECK nang
###    paulit-ulit sa production; kung itatala, matatabunan ang mahahalagang log
GET http://localhost:3000/api/health

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Rate limit (tingnan ang 08-rate-limit.http — i-send ang #3 nang 11 beses). Ang inaasahan sa terminal:
###    WARN Rate limit hit · event: "rate_limit" · requestId: X
###    WARN request completed · statusCode: 429 · requestId: X   ← PAREHONG ID, kaya magkadugtong
